        ("Heat pump or furnace in 2026? The honest version", """<p>With the credit gone, the up-front gap between a high-efficiency furnace and a cold-climate heat pump is wider than it was. A heat pump still wins on running cost in mild and moderate climates and anywhere electricity is cheap relative to gas; in very cold regions a dual-fuel setup (heat pump with a gas furnace backup) is the common compromise. If your AC is also near the end of its life, replacing both with one heat pump often costs less than two separate jobs and qualifies for the larger utility rebates. If only the furnace has failed, a like-for-like furnace is the smaller, faster, cheaper fix, and our guide to <a href="/blog/emergency-furnace-replacement/">emergency furnace replacement</a> covers that decision in detail.</p>"""),
        ("How to pay for a heat pump or HVAC system now", """<p>Four routes cover nearly every job. The <strong>contractor's financing plan</strong> is presented at the quote with a soft-pull pre-qualification; ask whether a promotional rate is deferred interest and whether the price is the same for cash. An <strong>unsecured HVAC loan</strong> you arrange yourself funds in days and pays any contractor like cash. <strong>Utility on-bill financing</strong>, where offered, adds the payment to your electric bill, sometimes at low rates. A <strong>home equity loan or HELOC</strong> suits a whole-house electrification project if you have equity and time. Our <a href="/hvac-financing/">HVAC financing</a> page compares them with example payments; if your credit is on the lower side, start with <a href="/hvac-financing/bad-credit-hvac-financing/">HVAC financing with bad credit</a>.</p>"""),
        ("Timing: why November still matters", """<p>Three reasons to move before winter rather than after a January failure. Contractors have capacity now and quote more competitively than during the first cold snap. Utility rebate budgets are often annual and some run out before December. And a planned install lets you check options with a soft pull from two or three sources instead of signing whatever is on the tablet at 9 pm. If your system is past 15 years and showing its age, get two quotes this month, run the rebate finder in the checklist below, and finance only what's left.</p>"""),
